"Fit the Library's line to this goal. The line below is what the Library runs for this kind of department. Keep every engine the goal needs, in the same order, and say, for an engine that should work differently for this goal, what it does differently. Leave an engine out only when no done-when item needs what it writes, and never one marked required."
"Shape the workflows this department needs to make every one of its done-when items true. Make the fewest engines that cover every item, usually two to five, in the order they run. Each engine reads one thing and writes one thing: the first reads the Brief (the owner's words), and each later one reads what an earlier one wrote. An engine that covers no item must feed one that does."
